cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these data, please cite the associated article."
title: "certus_re"
abstract: >-
  Reverse engineering of multilayer optical coatings from measured reflectance and
  transmittance spectra. Several samples are inverted jointly, sharing the coatings they
  have in common; two-side-coated components are handled with a coherent stack on each face
  and the substrate treated incoherently between them; the finite beam aperture is modelled
  as a piecewise-constant function of wavelength, stepped at the instrument's documented
  source and detector switchovers and imposed rather than fitted. Every run declares, counts
  and reports the parameter blocks it is allowed to move, so that a residual can be read
  next to the number of degrees of freedom that produced it. Includes the measured spectra
  of a six-layer antireflection coating, a seventeen-layer beam splitter, a two-side-coated
  component and two single-layer witnesses, all deposited on a Buhler Leybold Optics
  HELIOS 800 at Institut Fresnel.
type: software
